# Git Workflow

Canonical rule: **`.agents/rules/git-workflow.md`** — read it in full before acting. It is shared by every agent tool (Cursor, Claude Code, others); edit that file, not this pointer.

In one line: All changes go through a branch created from `main` and a PR; `main` is protected by a GitHub ruleset (PR + CI required, no bypass); one PR at a time, never stacked; squash merge; no AI attribution in commits or PRs.
